From 1531c59e78a16d7c6e5bbdeeabcc4bddf974cca6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:47:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: a 16 MiB context pool on MFC v10 behind an
 IOMMU

Each H.264 or HEVC decoder takes a 2 MiB context from the pool that
also holds the firmware. With 8 MiB only three decoders fit, and the
fourth fails in VIDIOC_REQBUFS with -ENOMEM ("Failed to allocate
instance buffer"), while Android's codec list advertises four
instances: a gallery that keeps the neighbouring pages' players open
and a thumbnail extractor are enough to reach it.

Use 16 MiB, which hold seven decoders, and allocate the pool under
32 MiB of IOVA instead of 16 MiB so that it fits.

Tested on Exynos7870 (MFC 0xa0b0): with eight contexts (next patch),
seven HEVC decoders open at once and the eighth fails in REQBUFS; four
decoders and four encoders open together.

---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
index 95547e66fe..1e3ed3d410 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
@@ -1292,6 +1292,15 @@ static int s5p_mfc_configure_common_memory(struct s5p_mfc_dev *mfc_dev)
 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DMA_CMA) || exynos_is_iommu_available(dev))
 		mem_size = SZ_8M;
 
+	/*
+	 * Every H.264 or HEVC decoder takes a 2 MiB context from this pool:
+	 * 8 MiB, less the firmware, hold three, and the fourth fails in
+	 * REQBUFS while the codec list advertises four instances. 16 MiB
+	 * hold seven.
+	 */
+	if (mfc_dev->variant->v10x_quirks && exynos_is_iommu_available(dev))
+		mem_size = SZ_16M;
+
 	if (mfc_mem_size)
 		mem_size = memparse(mfc_mem_size, NULL);
 
@@ -1303,11 +1312,12 @@ static int s5p_mfc_configure_common_memory(struct s5p_mfc_dev *mfc_dev)
 	 * The firmware addresses memory as offsets from its base: every
 	 * buffer must lie above it. The IOMMU DMA allocator hands out
 	 * addresses top down, so the firmware, allocated first, would end
-	 * up above everything else. Allocate it under 16 MiB, then keep the
-	 * video buffers within 256 MiB, above it.
+	 * up above everything else. Allocate it under 32 MiB, right above
+	 * the 16 MiB the device tree reserves, then keep the video buffers
+	 * within 256 MiB, above it.
 	 */
 	if (mfc_dev->variant->v10x_quirks && exynos_is_iommu_available(dev))
-		dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(24));
+		dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(25));
 
 	mfc_dev->mem_virt = dma_alloc_coherent(dev, mem_size,
 					       &mfc_dev->mem_base, GFP_KERNEL);
-- 
